From af10f71038df3a886001f61c90f5753fb2096ea4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:30:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06928/11362] [outer-loop] bp35: L7 SOLVED round 11 (codex,
 first attempt at fresh territory)

Round-11 gpt-5.6-sol session solved L7 on the first attempt. L7
doubles the per-level hard timer from L6's 64 actions to 128 -- the
session grounded this via the executable timer branch rather than
assuming it carries over. L7 is a deliberate temporary-support puzzle:
open X-cells must be solidified above the player to create an
intermediate landing altitude, several toggled twice at different
route phases, unlocking lateral transfers impossible from either
natural shelf.

The source agent's own fresh-environment reproduction gate confirmed
reached_level=7 independently. The outer loop independently
re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=7,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED (frame well-formed, not degenerate).

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: bp35 levels_reproduced 6 -> 7.
reproducible_total_levels 173 -> 174 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
